Current original Zero workflow (0.12)

Use the native tools on Linux or their .exe versions on Windows:
  zero-integrate PROJECT_DIRECTORY NEW_KERNEL.zero
  zero-build PROJECT_DIRECTORY NEW_OUTPUT_DIRECTORY NEW_KERNEL.zero
  zero-check PROJECT_DIRECTORY NEW_TEST_DIRECTORY
All destination paths must be new. The integrator preserves authored sources;
the builder checks its compiler fixed point and builds the original targets;
the verifier checks language behavior and host file operations in process.
See tools/integrate.ztext, tools/build.ztext and checks/README.ztext.
Read these documents with zero-text read FILE.

The notes below preserve earlier implementation and test history. Any old
shell/Python runner names, generated artifacts, JSON reports or commands are
historical references: they were removed from the active project and are not
current runnable instructions or current-release validation. Native host
checks do not replace BIOS/UEFI, persistence or physical-hardware testing.

Historical implementation notes

Zero WiFi work status - 2026-11-16

Implemented in original Zero (no downloaded code): bounded modal state machine,
automatic PCI-discovery handoff, one-based card/network navigation, bounded
ASCII renderer, 8..63-character masked password entry, backspace, cancellation,
secret erasure on close and every completed connection, and generation-tagged
backend request/reply interface. Production PCI detection is integrated by the
wired network worker. Kernel keyboard/modal integration is owned by the root
agent. Four UI parts compile successfully with the own compiler for hosted,
raw64 and raw32 targets. The isolated harness remains below23KiB raw32 and
16KiB raw64, including test declarations and initialization.

Normal UI wording now uses plain connection/setup/search language. Unsupported
hardware and unverified Internet access remain explicit; every simulated
backend screen retains the visible SIMULATION / NO RADIO / NO PACKETS label.

26 executed behavioral fixtures pass: detection/no-adapter/unsupported,
one-card automatic selection, both selection bounds, network choice,
password masking/backspace/63-byte limit/short-password refusal, open-network
connection path, pending/success/auth-failure states, and cancellation before
and during connection, stale-generation replies, empty scans, failed scans
and an invalid9-network result. Every fixture checks secret-tail zeroing, full
secret erasure on completion/close and memory-boundary guards. Fifteen original Zero
rendered1920x1080 screenshots cover all meaningful UI stages, plus production
no-radio/unsupported outcomes, in net/wifi-fixtures/*.png. See results.txt
there and reproduce with python3 net/wifi-test.py. Python only orchestrates
and losslessly encodes the Zero-produced PPM as PNG.

No native WiFi chipset driver, 802.11 management/data path, WPA2 supplicant or
radio firmware loader currently exists. Detected class0280 controllers must
remain unsupported. They do not produce invented SSIDs or connection success.
USB/SDIO radio discovery is not implemented. Standard QEMU emulated Ethernet
connected through a host's WiFi/NAT is not a native guest WiFi device.

The hosted fixture backend is explicitly labeled SIMULATION / NO RADIO /
NO PACKETS on every screen. It exists to execute and inspect the genuine UI
state machine, including the stages that unsupported production hardware
cannot enter. Its success screenshots are not radio/network evidence.

Chipset feasibility: a real Intel/Atheros/Realtek PCI radio requires a device-
specific control/DMA path, firmware where applicable, 802.11 scan and
association, and WPA2 key establishment/encryption. None may be replaced by
an Ethernet link-state check or by fixture replies. This work provides the
honest discovery and application/driver boundary, not those absent layers.
No radio hardware was made available to this subtask. Existing VM network
devices are Ethernet; the root VM verifier is checking emulator capabilities
and actual PCI detection. Unsupported cases remain usable and cancellable.
